The Guidebook only mentions wishing in the context of the conduct of not
doing it; I don't know that I'd be in favour of its getting specific in
terms of "this is how you should phrase your wishes".

(Understanding English numbers would probably be a good thing, though,
yes; presumably there's fairly drop-in code out there that can parse
"two", "three thousand and six", "a hundred and twenty-seven", "two
hundred sixty-three" (you'd want to handle both American and British
dialect forms). The number of zorkmids you can successfully wish for
at a time (in normal mode) maxes at 5000, so there's no need to
accurately parse anything higher than that (though you do need to
recognise that "a hundred and one thousand" _is_ higher than that, and
not 1100).)

